    {
      "id": "claim_c678e9d61a4e409d88c24c9ac7944851",
      "statement": "A generation is everything a node derives from a deployment — compiled Worker configurations, isolate pools, the Durable Object class registry, service bindings, asset resolvers, and cron schedule — and a request that started on one generation finishes on it even after the node adopts another.",
